## Executive Summary

NOT public-ready; internal dogfood is close but gated. Verdict at HEAD 755bf3846. PUBLIC-BETA is blocked by three independently-confirmed classes: (1) install path — the committed .mcp.json:25 hardcodes /Users/hue/plugins/dopemux-mission-control/scripts/task-orchestrator-current-stdio.sh with no installer rewrite, so the task-orchestrator MCP is dead on every non-author clone; (2) multi-instance safety — no per-instance Redis (instance_overlay.write_compose_override never remaps redis-primary) and ADHD-engine keys are user-scoped only, so two worktrees for the same user collide on attention/break/profile state; (3) cold-start races — compose.yml uses condition: service_started (bare-list depends_on) for conport/task-orchestrator/adhd-engine. INTERNAL-BETA is gated by RV-3 (the `decisions` CLI group ships only energy+patterns; review/list/show/update-outcome/query are absent) and by the agent-wrapping live-run path being UNASSESSABLE (the AGENT-WRAPPING SPEC arrived empty {} — no work_breakdown was provided, so I cannot fold wrapping build-items in or confirm that codex/copilot/claude/vanilla wrapping actually runs). A known regression is also live: PR #720 stripped the orchestrator /dx: command surface — .claude/commands/dx/ now contains only implement.md (Wave 0 restore). Re-verification CLEARED several inherited fears: RV-2 (routing NameError) is genuinely fixed, RV-6 (litellm hard-import) is fixed, RV-10 has a stop_hook_active re-entry guard so it is friction not a hard lockup, and MCP-9's worktree-isolation residual is refuted because ConPort's _ensure_schema() idempotently adds instance_id at boot. Top risks to close first: clean-machine install (task-orchestrator path), then the dual data-integrity gaps (Redis multi-instance + startup races), then RV-3.

