- No orchestrator config.yaml under .claude (`find .claude -iname '*orchestr*'` returns only runtime hook artifacts .orchestrator-edit-nudge*.json / .orchestrator-context-cache.json, not the command surface or config)
- `git log` shows #720 (d8e0268d3 family) merged; matches durable memory [palette-clobber-main-2026-05-28] 'verified at main 755bf3846'
- Recovery source per memory: `origin/task-orchestrator-claude-surface` (branch not present in this worktree's refs)

### Hooks

#### BETA-HOOK-01 — Stop hook blocks session exit once per stop when a workflow is active and no checkpoint/completion-token emitted (friction, not hard lockup) (LOW, polish)

> Only bites a user who tries to end the session mid dopemux-workflow with no emitted checkpoint. The block fires once, then `stop_hook_active` lets the next exit through, so it is recoverable confusion rather than a lockup. For polish, add an explicit `dopemux workflow abandon` escape or a time/iteration-based auto-release so the first block isn't surprising. Low priority for internal beta.

- `src/dopemux/claude/native_hooks.py:370-373` — `_on_stop` returns `_block_stop` (EXIT_BLOCK) when workflow active and not stop-safe
- `src/dopemux/claude/native_hooks.py:347-348` — but `if data.get('stop_hook_active') is True: return self._allow()` — Claude Code's re-entry signal lets the 2nd Stop pass, preventing a permanent trap
- `src/dopemux/claude/native_hooks.py:344-345` — no active workflow → `_allow` immediately (vanilla users unaffected)
- `src/dopemux/claude/native_hooks.py:355,361,364` — checkpoint/completion-token escape paths exist; no time-based timeout
- Narrows inherited RV-10 (PARTIAL): re-entry guard exists, so not the trap originally described

### Cleanup (post-beta, confirmed)

#### BETA-CLEAN-01 — Remove dead/stub services: `services/router` (only `__init__`) and `services/dope-query` (no server) (OBS, post-beta)

> These two service directories have no runnable server and no compose service. They add navigation noise and imply capability that does not exist. Delete them (or move to an explicit `/experiments` area). NOTE: dope-memory is NOT in this set — it is an active service (compose builds it from services/working-memory-assistant/Dockerfile.dope-memory and ships mcp_stdio_adapter.py); the inherited 'dope-memory duplicates working-memory-assistant' claim is refuted.

- `services/router/` — only `__init__.py` (version string + service-name constant, no implementation)
- `services/dope-query/` — only `auth/models.py` + `tests/test_password_utils.py`, no server/main/MCP entry
- Confirmed by both inherited RV-11 and MCP-8 (2 sources)

#### BETA-MCP-04 — Document shared-Postgres single-role/dev-credential posture; confirm migration 007 ordering for advanced graph features (OBS, post-beta)

> Data-plane isolation for ConPort holds on a fresh install (workspace_id is a partition key; active_context is per (workspace_id, instance_id) via _ensure_schema-added column). Two doc items remain: (1) all services share one Postgres role/DB with dev-default credentials — fine for single-tenant local, must be hardened/documented before any shared deployment; (2) document which migrations beyond instance_id are auto-applied vs require manual run, since start_with_info.sh has no migration step.

- `compose.yml:245-246` — ConPort DATABASE_URL/POSTGRES_URL hardcoded to dopemux-postgres-age/dopemux_knowledge_graph with dev-default creds (not instance-parameterized)
- `compose.yml:471,477` dope-memory and :371 dopecon-bridge share the same Postgres role/DB
- `docker/mcp-servers-source/conport/enhanced_server.py:408,480-481` — `_ensure_schema()` runs `ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS instance_id` at boot (so worktree-isolation residual from inherited MCP-9 is REFUTED — instance_id is auto-applied; the standalone 007 SQL is not the only path)
- `docker/mcp-servers-source/conport/start_with_info.sh` — launches servers only, no migration step (so anything NOT covered by `_ensure_schema` must be applied manually)

