## Likely Resolved

- **RV-2 (routing mode NameError)** — RE-VERIFIED RESOLVED/certain at this HEAD: routing_cli.py:548-569 `_set_routing_mode` uses loaded/rendered/mode cleanly with no undefined `content`; callers at :190,:221 pass (config_path, mode); group registered via cli.py:6129-6142.
- **RV-6 (mobile/tmux hard-require litellm)** — RE-VERIFIED RESOLVED/high: src/dopemux/mobile/cli.py and mobile/runtime.py import only config + tmux.common + tmux.controller; tmux/controller.py and tmux/common.py have no litellm import. The litellm tokens in tmux/cli.py are env-var name strings (LITELLM_MASTER_KEY etc.), not Python imports.
- **MCP-0 (Qdrant cross-project index poisoning)** — inherited REFUTED; not re-investigated, no contradicting evidence surfaced.
- **MCP-1 (Redis user-scoped not workspace-scoped)** — same fact as RV-7; disposition upgraded — re-verify (RV-7 / BETA-MCP-03) supersedes it as a live public-beta multi-instance item. Listed here to avoid double-counting as a separate blocker.
- **MCP-2 (multi-instance detection probes wrong port)** — inherited REFUTED; not re-investigated.
- **MCP-5 (two contradictory port-offset schemes)** — inherited REFUTED; not re-investigated.
- **MCP-7 (mcp-proxy config still registers mas-sequential-thinking)** — inherited REFUTED; not re-investigated.
- **MCP-9 worktree-isolation RESIDUAL (requires migration 007 to have run)** — REFUTED at this HEAD: enhanced_server.py:176 calls `_ensure_schema()` which at :480-481 runs `ALTER TABLE ... ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS instance_id` idempotently at boot, and active_context read/write at :501-564 is fully instance-aware. The shared-credentials documentation note from MCP-9 is retained as post_beta BETA-MCP-04.
- **RV-10 (Stop hook traps user)** — narrowed, not fully resolved: re-entry guard (native_hooks.py:347-348) prevents a hard trap; retained as LOW-severity friction item BETA-HOOK-01 rather than a blocker.

