- **AGENT-WRAPPING live-run path**: the AGENT-WRAPPING SPEC input was empty (`{}`), so no work_breakdown was provided. I could not assess whether codex/copilot/claude/vanilla agent wrapping actually executes end-to-end, nor fold wrapping build-items into the backlog. This blocks a confident internal-beta GO until the wrapping path is exercised and its tasks enumerated. (See `03-AGENT-WRAPPING-SPEC.md`.)
- **BETA-MCP-01 single-vs-dual-gate**: whether the dogfood launcher ALWAYS exports `CONPORT_MCP_PORT`/`DOPE_MEMORY_PORT` before Claude Code starts is unconfirmed. `instance_overlay.write_mcp_env` emits them, but I did not trace every launch entrypoint. If the launcher is guaranteed-first, BETA-MCP-01 is public-only; otherwise it is also internal. Kept on both gates conservatively.
- **BETA-SURF-01 recovery completeness**: `origin/task-orchestrator-claude-surface` (the restore source named in durable memory) is not present in this worktree's refs, so I could not diff the exact set of deleted `/dx:` files + orchestrator config.yaml against HEAD. The regression is confirmed (only implement.md remains under `.claude/commands/dx/`) but the precise restore manifest is unverified.
- **ConPort `_ensure_schema` coverage**: `_ensure_schema()` auto-adds instance_id, but I did not enumerate every column/index the standalone migrations 002/003/007 create. Whether any advanced graph feature depends on a migration NOT covered by `_ensure_schema` (and thus silently missing on fresh installs, since start_with_info.sh runs no migration step) is unverified — captured in BETA-MCP-04.
